WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.169
-We've met on this show.
-We did.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:07.139
-Not too long ago.
We played musical beers.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.674
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.443
What else do you remember
about that?

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.778
-We got very close, you and I.
We did.

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:14.214
-Yeah. We kind of did.

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.547
I have a --
-We made out.

00:00:15.547 --> 00:00:18.350
-We -- No, we didn't.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.653
No.
-It was close.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.021
-Well, let me show you.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.789
Here's a clip of us playing
musical beers on our show.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:25.324
Take a look at this.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:26.593
-Oh, [bleep]!

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.394
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:29.863
[Bleep]

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.865
-Spin it back! Spin it back!

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.970
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.909
-We gotta drink that, baby.
I'll gladly lose.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:47.046
[ Crowd chanting "Drink" ]

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:51.350
♪♪

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.019
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.086
Oh, my God. Yes!

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:56.188
-The commitment.
-The commitment.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:57.624
We had to.
-It was good.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.059
It was for the audience.
Yeah. Had to show you.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.461
Hey. Everyone's welcome here.
-I appreciate it.

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.864
-Gosh, that was bizarre
to watch that back.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.133
-No, it was -- it was --
Here's what happened.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.101
I mean, I was before --
Right before I came on,

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.537
you know, my manager, my great
manager, Emily Gerson Saines,

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:14.774
was backstage, and the thing
she said to me was, like,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:19.144
"Whatever you do,
do not be the first one out."

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:20.847
She was like -- And I was like,

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.648
"Why are you doing this
to me right now?"

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.484
She was like, "Just don't lose.
Don't be the first one out."

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:28.454
So I came in, you know, strong.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.223
-[ Laughs ]
-A little too strong.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.592
-Yeah, a little too strong.
No, it was perfect.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.827
We're happy to you have back.
-Thank you.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.131
You went on to -- Congrats
on "Avengers: Endgame."

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.600
This movie is...

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.802
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.205
$1.4 billion it's made so far.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.207
Wow.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.743
Does it change -- Does your life
change completely?

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.011
-Well, it has --
You know, for me, I mean,

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:55.748
it's been ten years,
so it's a little bit nostalgic,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.917
but it's only been since last
year and "Infinity War"

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.119
that, like, I've sort of been
feeling like I'm in this

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.154
Fight Club that I don't
really know about.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:05.825
I was on a plane one time,
and the stewardess came

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.328
and gave me this piece of paper
and walked away,

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.364
and I opened it,
and it said "Wakanda Forever."

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.901
And then I looked, after, down
the hall, and she just went...

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:19.772
-Wow! Wow!
-I was like, "Just get us home."

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.541
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.744
But it's very humbling,
for sure, just to be included.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.946
I mean, the movie is insane.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.682
-It's great. You're history.
Absolutely.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.384
But when you're filming
the scenes, do you know

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.253
what you're even remotely doing
or what lines you're saying?

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:36.855
-We did not.
For this one, we didn't.

00:02:36.855 --> 00:02:40.159
I mean, everything I filmed,
I found out on the day.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.595
You can kind of tell, like,
by my expression.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.930
I just --
I hide the confusion well.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.133
Under a "Zoolander" look.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.769
But, no, we didn't know.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.605
-Like when you were in there
with all of your co-stars,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.575
did you know that they were
going to be there that day?

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.177
-No. I was told
there was a wedding.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.014
You know, that there was
a wedding that we were filming.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.115
And I was like,
"Who's getting married?"

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.151
But everybody
was dressed very formal,

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:07.119
and, you know,
I was looking around,

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.722
and then two people
weren't there,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.691
so I guess that was
the bride and the groom.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.327
But that's what it was.
It was a wedding.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.697
You saw the movie, right?
It was a wedding.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.232
-Yeah, of course, it was.
-That's what it was.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.735
-Yes, of course. Oh, yeah.
Sebastian, absolutely, it was.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.771
I'll never get you in trouble.
Yeah, of course.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.406
But now I got to say --

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:30.977
I just heard this, and I hope
that the rumor is true,

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.846
that Anthony Mackie,
who's Falcon --

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.181
-Oh, he's great.

00:03:36.181 --> 00:03:38.951
-He's the most fun human being.
We love Anthony Mackie.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.786
We've had him on our show
since "Late Night,"

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.122
and I heard that you and him
are getting a spin-off --

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.258
You're getting a series
on Disney+.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.892
-That's the word, yeah.

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:50.263
It only took
about four press tours

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.198
for somebody to kind of
get the idea

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.900
that these two lunatics
should have a show, you know?

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.703
-Yeah.
So the rumors are true?

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.972
-The rumors are --
The rumors are true.

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:03.142
Yeah.
-I didn't even believe that.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.011
You're doing it so well.
-No, they are.

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:08.780
I mean, I love him because,
like, it's really hard.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.484
Like, I always quote "Apollo 13"
every time I'm with him

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.519
because, it's, like,
working with him

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.221
is really like riding
a psychotic horse

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.322
in a blazing stable.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.424
Like, that's what it is.
I just hang on.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.292
And usually
if you look at my expressions,

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:22.194
like, just get a word in now.

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:25.198
-I have a clip here from a press
junket that you guys were doing.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:27.233
Can you explain
what he kept doing?

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.801
'Cause it's ridiculous.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.437
-Right.
-The name?

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:35.074
-Yeah, he -- So, you know,
like, we do this a lot.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.776
I mean, you're in there

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.745
for, you know, three,
four days at a time.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:41.414
-Days of the same questions?

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.949
-Yeah, the same questions, and
you can't really spoil anything.

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.417
You can't talk about the movie.

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:48.353
So after a while, we kind of
start having fun with it.

00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:51.024
And he and I sort of, like,
invented this character

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.059
that we sort of, kind of,
came up with.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.194
So that any time they would ask
us a serious question,

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.263
like, you know, especially
in the European pressers,

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.965
like,
"How do you feel this movie

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.367
is really going to
change the world?"

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.870
And we're like,
"Well, as my friend...

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.105
-Is it Nishka?
-...Ishtata used to say..."

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.007
-And so you'd just
make up a name?

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.209
-Yeah, and then we're like --
We'd say something obscure

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.378
like, "When you look
in the mirror, make sure

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:17.016
you look in the back
and the front at the same time."

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.952
"That's what my friend..."
-And they're like, "Right."

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.821
"I wouldn't say it,
but that's what --

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.956
My friend Ishna would say that."

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:27.393
I have a clip, kind of
a compilation of you playing.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:28.728
It's so funny.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.929
Here are Sebastian
and Anthony Mackie

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:33.232
doing press for
"Captain America: Civil War."

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.767
Take a look at this.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:38.236
-As my friend Nish would say,
always enjoy the pants you're in

00:05:38.236 --> 00:05:40.339
because you never know
what's in another man's pants.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.542
-That's right.
-As my friend Nishka would say,

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.611
I ain't saying
I'm a gold digger, but I am.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.413
-But he rich.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.882
-I think when you have
two beautiful people

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.183
and you put them together,

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:53.486
there's nothing bad
that can come out of that.

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:56.255
-What a lovely last answer.
-That's not me.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.291
-Thank you so much.
-That's Nishka.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.025
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.025 --> 00:06:03.696
-I'm looking forward to more
goof-offs with you and Anthony.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.032
We love you. Sebastian Stan!

